$ gragas journal recover --help
--- exit 0
--- stdout

  A run that was killed after its first
  write has a record
  with no close. recover puts every file
  of each such run back
  from the copies its record kept, under
  the folder's lock, and
  closes the record as rolled back. It
  never finishes a run:
  plan it again. Without --apply it
  lists the runs it would
  roll back and writes nothing.

    gragas journal recover
    gragas journal recover --apply

  USAGE


    gragas journal recover [--flags]


  FLAGS

    --accessible  Plain questions
                  (ACCESSIBLE)
    --apply       Write the files
    --config      The settings file
                  (GRAGAS_CONFIG)
    -h --help     Help for recover
    --json        Answer in one JSON
                  document
    --no-color    No colour (NO_COLOR)
    --plain       Print plainly: nothing
                  moves

--- stderr
